lisa-design:
- Limits verified against Renovate 44.145.1 source (lib/workers/global/limits.ts, process/write.ts, process/limits.ts, update/pr/index.ts, update/branch/index.ts): calcLimit takes the lowest limit across a branch's upgrades and any 0/null makes the branch unlimited; ConcurrentPRs counts open non-vulnerability Renovate PRs, HourlyPRs counts ALL Renovate PRs created this clock hour (vulnerability ones included) and is incremented on each creation.
- Consequence kept on purpose (spec): the majors rule's prHourlyLimit 1 means a major opens only in an hour with no other Renovate PR yet, so none in a visit that opens the non-major group or a security PR; docs say so rather than claiming "group + 1 major per visit". prHourlyLimit 2 on majors was rejected: with no group due it would allow 2 majors a visit.
- vulnerabilityAlerts prConcurrentLimit/branchConcurrentLimit 0 rather than a large number: 0 short-circuits calcLimit to unlimited, and vulnerabilityAlerts is applied over packageRules, so a major security fix does not inherit the majors rule's 3. renovate-config-validator 44.145.1 --strict accepts both keys there (and rejects a misspelt key there, so the keys are really validated).
- TestSharedPreset also fails if any rule other than the majors rule sets prConcurrentLimit/prHourlyLimit: through lowest-limit-wins such a limit would cap the non-major group or a security fix.
- TestThrottle bound is MaxLiveRepos x prHourlyLimit (60), a worst case; MaxLiveRepos stays 15 (also keeps a live run within the app token's hour). ccf-bump-sync.yml and its 8th/22nd schedule are untouched.
